yorkshire in northern england  four hours by car from london  here guests at the rudding park hotel  can make the most of the bucolic  surroundings  whether playing a round of golf  or sampling some of yorkshire's finest  cuisine  people come from far near to enjoy the  traditional english sunday roast  today one of the hotel's 20 chefs  matthew wilkinson is going to let us in  on the secret of the region's most  famous dish yorkshire pudding  not to be confused uh with with it with  a pudding or dessert it's basically a  batter which says eggs flour and milk  mixed together cooked in a very hot oven  and traditionally served with um  roast beef  rutting park even has a resident expert  stephanie moon gives the chefs tips on  recipes and ingredients  first of all she recommends regional  products  today she's buying yorkshire pudding  ingredients at the local farm shop  the last five ten years have seen such a  revival of farm shops because people are  wanting to buy local produce they want  to buy freshly made bread they want to  buy free-range eggs from down the road  food miles is very important and  something that you know we're all  starting to take more and more notice of  she even buys the meat for the roast  here  back in the hotel kitchen matthew  wilkinson has the oven ready and waiting  at 210 degrees celsius  whisk flour eggs and milk together in a  large bowl to form a smooth batter  pour through a sieve to get rid of every  last lamp grease a muffin tin with oil  and heat it for five minutes in the oven  if you want to do that then you just end  up with a really small  yoshi pudding and also when it rises you  get a nice hole in the middle  which is where you put the gravy at the  end  quickly pour the batter into the  sizzling hot oil  then return the tin to the oven and cook  for half an hour until your perfect pud  is formed hollow puffed up and golden  brown  it's nice and hollow inside and that's  where we're going to pour the gravy it's  gonna soak up into the extra pudding  it's gonna nicely use out when you cut  into it  for the roast beef season the meat  generously with salt pepper and sprigs  of thyme  roast at 220 degrees celsius in a  preheated oven for around 45 minutes to  an hour depending on its weight  dinner is served  perfectly cooked roast beef and  yorkshire pudding with roast potatoes  and gravy  and now it's time for the taste test  yorkshire cuisine expert stephanie moon  and journalist elaine lam are ready and  waiting  lem has written a book about the humble  roots of yorkshire pudding  back then only the rich ate the meat  but the poorer people got to eat the  batter pudding from underneath which is  what became a yorkshire pudding it was  full of the flavor of the meat the  drippings from the meat and it's kind of  stuck with it the two have gone together  for centuries  these days yorkshire pudding can be  enjoyed by all  in fact the roast beef's tasty  accompaniment often steals the show  yorkshire pudding a british culinary  classic and not too tricky to try at  home
 

